.TH LIFE-WALLPAPER 1 "October 2026" "life-wallpaper 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
life-wallpaper \- Conway's Game of Life as a native Wayland wallpaper
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B life-wallpaper
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B life-wallpaper
runs an animated cellular-automaton wallpaper on Wayland compositors that support
.BR zwlr_layer_shell_v1 .
It can manage all outputs, react to output hotplugging, and reload configuration
changes while running.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -h , " " --help
Print command-line help and exit.
.TP
.BR -o , " " --output " " NAME
Render only on the named output. By default, all outputs are used.
.TP
.B --list-outputs
Print detected output names, make/model, logical size, and scale, then exit.
.TP
.BI --config " PATH"
Read configuration from PATH. If omitted, the default is
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/life-wallpaper/config.toml
or
.IR $HOME/.config/life-wallpaper/config.toml .
If the selected file does not exist, the application attempts to create it from
the bundled default configuration.
.TP
.BI --preset " NAME"
Start with one of the built-in configuration presets: 
.BR default ,
.BR ambient ,
.BR matrix-rain ,
.BR neon-brain , or
.BR minimal .
Preset values are loaded first, values in an existing config file override the
preset, and command-line options override both. If a config file is missing, it
is created from the default template but does not override the selected preset
on that first run.
.TP
.BI --cell-size " PX"
Cell size in logical pixels (2 to 64; default 8).
.TP
.BI --fps " HZ"
Generations per second (0.1 to 60; default 4).
.TP
.BI --density " VALUE"
Initial and reseed population density (0 to 1; default 0.25; also sets reseed density).
.TP
.BI --rule " RULE"
Automaton rule: 
.BR life ,
.BR highlife ,
.BR daynight ,
.BR seeds ,
.BR brain ,
.BR rotate , or a rule in B/S notation such as
.BR B3/S23 .
.TP
.BI --color " COLOR"
Use age-based coloring or a fixed named color (green, yellow, orange, red, aqua,
blue, purple) or a hex color such as
.BR #rrggbb .
.TP
.B --[no-]trail
Enable or disable fading trails from dead cells.
.TP
.B --[no-]rain
Enable or disable faint hex code-rain behind the cells.
.TP
.B --[no-]overlay
Enable or disable the generation/population status line.
.TP
.B --[no-]sysload
Enable or disable CPU-load-driven speed, sparks, and heat.
.TP
.B --[no-]patterns
Enable or disable periodic pattern injections.
.TP
.B --[no-]stamps
Enable or disable periodic logo and text stamps.
.PP
The board is not wiped on a timer. When it goes calm for
.B stagnation_secs
(moving or chaotic cells below
.B calm_pct
percent of the grid, or the whole board repeating), new life is added on top of
the existing cells. The optional
.B soft_reset_secs
timer is off by default (0).
.PP
Other supported configuration keys can be set in the TOML file. See
.BR config_example/config.default.toml
for the complete list and comments.
.PP
When settled shapes cover
.B clutter_pct
percent of the grid, whole shapes are pruned instead of resetting the board.
.SS Smoothness, look and persistence
.TP
.B smooth, render_fps
Crossfade cells between generations at up to
.B render_fps
frames per second (default on, 30). Only changing cells are redrawn.
.TP
.B pause_hidden
Stop simulating and drawing while the compositor is not showing the wallpaper
(a fullscreen window on top, screen off); detected through Wayland frame callbacks.
.TP
.B cell_gap, cell_round
Pixels between cells (default 1) and rounded corners (default on).
.TP
.B persist, save_secs
Save each output's board under
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/life-wallpaper/
on exit and every
.B save_secs
seconds, and restore it at start.
.SH PRESETS
.TP
.B default
Balanced default colors and animation.
.TP
.B ambient
Slower, calmer animation with fewer visual elements.
.TP
.B matrix-rain
Green palette, code-rain effect, and status overlay.
.TP
.B neon-brain
Fast Brian's Brain simulation with a neon palette.
.TP
.B minimal
Uncluttered appearance without trails, rain, overlays, patterns, or stamps.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The configuration file is checked on each animation tick. Saving changes applies
them without restarting the wallpaper. A
.B SIGHUP
also triggers a reload:
.PP
.RS
.nf
pkill -HUP life-wallpaper
.fi
.RE
.PP
Configuration values are loaded in this order: built-in defaults, selected
preset, config file, then command-line flags. Later sources override earlier ones.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Start with the ambient preset:
.B life-wallpaper --preset ambient
.TP
Use Matrix Rain on one output:
.B life-wallpaper --preset matrix-rain --output DP-1
.TP
Use a preset and override its frame rate:
.B life-wallpaper --preset neon-brain --fps 6
.TP
Use a custom configuration file:
.B life-wallpaper --config ~/.config/life-wallpaper/work.toml
.TP
List available outputs:
.B life-wallpaper --list-outputs
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory for the default configuration path.
.TP
.B HOME
Used to derive the default configuration path when XDG_CONFIG_HOME is unset.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Reload the selected configuration file.
.TP
.B SIGINT, SIGTERM
Shut down cleanly.
.SH NOTES
Requires a Wayland compositor with the wlr layer-shell protocol. The program is
not intended for X11 sessions without a compatible Wayland environment.
